.TH CWE-93 7 "2026-11-15" "CWE Top 25 (2025)" "Software Weakness Reference"
.SH NAME
CWE\-93 \- Improper Neutralization of CRLF Sequences ('CRLF Injection')
.SH RANK
KEV\-referenced weakness. Not part of the 2025 CWE Top 25; documented here because it appears in the CISA KEV catalog.
.SH CLASSIFICATION
Class: KEV\-referenced weakness.
.SH DESCRIPTION
The product uses CRLF (carriage return line feeds) as a special element, e.g. to separate lines or records, but it does not neutralize or incorrectly neutralizes CRLF sequences from inputs.
.SH KNOWN EXPLOITED VULNERABILITIES
CISA KEV catalog (as of 2026-11-15): \fB1\fR exploited CVE mapped to this weakness. Each entry has the catalog write\-up of how it was used in the wild (not a runnable exploit) and the required remediation. Code\-level vulnerable\->fixed pairs, when curated, are under \fBEXAMPLES\fR.
.SS CVE\-2022\-27924
Synacor Zimbra Collaboration Suite (ZCS), added 2022\-08\-04, ransomware: Known.
.PP
Synacor Zimbra Collaboration Suite (ZCS) Command Injection Vulnerability.
.PP
\fIHow it is exploited (CISA):\fR
Synacor Zimbra Collaboration Suite (ZCS) allows an attacker to inject memcache commands into a targeted instance which causes an overwrite of arbitrary cached entries.
.PP
\fIRemediation:\fR
Apply updates per vendor instructions.
 Due 2022\-08\-25.
.PP
